{
  "id": "DP12Z",
  "version": "2.0",
  "title": "Local tumor excision",
  "description": "Local tumor excision is surgical removal of a skin cancer or tumor along with a margin of healthy tissue around it. Your dermatologic surgeon removes the tumor completely to eliminate cancer cells while preserving healthy skin. The size and location of the tumor determine the surgical technique used. Pathology examination of the removed specimen confirms complete removal. The wound is closed with stitches. The cost of this procedure may vary depending on the size of the area being treated. Categories include small (<3 cm), medium (2-5 cm), large (≥5 cm), and breast & radical resection.",
